5. Code-Level Observation

The application handles the Aspose exception approximately as follows:

try {
    pdfEditor1.resizeContents(doc1, new int[]{i}, params);
} catch (Exception e) {
    LOGGER.warn(
        "Skipping resize for page {} due to Aspose error: {}",
        i,
        e.getMessage()
    );
}

The important behavior is:

Aspose exception
      ↓
Exception caught
      ↓
Warning logged
      ↓
Method continues

There is no evidence from the reviewed flow that the entire source PDF is immediately marked as invalid and excluded from the final merge.

This is the main reason the partial PDF processing behavior does not fully isolate the problematic PDF.

